# __STOCHAFLOW_PROJECT_SLUG__

This repository is a standard Python distribution containing one Stochaflow
extension and room for multiple experiments. Stochaflow discovers the installed
extension through Python package metadata; it does not scan this directory.

Run commands from this project root so relative `data/` and `outputs/` paths in
experiment configuration resolve predictably.

## Install with pip

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -e ".[test]"
stochaflow train --config experiments/example/train.yaml
```

On Windows, activate the environment with `.venv\Scripts\activate`.

## Install with uv

```bash
uv sync --extra test
uv run stochaflow train --config experiments/example/train.yaml
```

The generated configuration trains a tiny synthetic regression model in a few
steps. It demonstrates a custom `DataBuilder`, model, `TrainingBuilder` and
`TrainingStrategy`, plus a direct-transform `SamplingBuilder`. The built-in MSE
objective and tensor artifact writer are reused.

The package entry point imports `__STOCHAFLOW_PACKAGE_NAME__.stochaflow_ext`.
Keep that aggregation module free of data loading, model construction, and task
execution: importing it should only define and register extension components.

Run the extension tests with either `python -m pytest` or `uv run pytest`.
